== B. Light laptops: one-shot ingest, then a 3k-token answer (local prefill burst / sustained x0.6) vs hybrid
   calibration: M6 measurement implies 16.2 TFLOP/s effective; earlier v4 assumed 4.8 for the M5 Air
  MacBook Air 13 M5 32 GB, $1,699 (153 GB/s, 12.4 TFLOP/s effective burst): burst rate scaled from the M6 measurement; sustained x0.6-0.8
    Qwen3.8-27B (AA 52.0)      context room ~304k; decode <= 8 tok/s; 3k answer 6.2 min
        8k: local   0.6 /   1.0 min | hybrid 100M  0.5 min, 200M    16 s, 1G    3 s | download 0.34 GB
       32k: local   2.6 /   4.3 min | hybrid 100M  1.7 min, 200M    52 s, 1G   11 s | download 1.13 GB
       70k: local   6.4 /  10.6 min | hybrid 100M  3.6 min, 200M   109 s, 1G   25 s | download 2.37 GB
    Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (AA 32.1)  context room ~547k; decode <= 55 tok/s; 3k answer 0.9 min
        8k: local   0.1 /   0.1 min | hybrid 100M  0.2 min, 200M     5 s, 1G    1 s | download 0.11 GB
       32k: local   0.4 /   0.6 min | hybrid 100M  0.5 min, 200M    16 s, 1G    3 s | download 0.36 GB
       70k: local   1.1 /   1.8 min | hybrid 100M  1.1 min, 200M    34 s, 1G    7 s | download 0.75 GB
  MacBook Air 13 M5 24 GB, $1,499 (153 GB/s, 12.4 TFLOP/s effective burst): as above; 27B leaves room for ~30K context (measured on a 24 GB M6)
    Qwen3.8-27B (AA 52.0)      context room ~60k; decode <= 8 tok/s; 3k answer 6.2 min
